# Description
In this challenge, you are given a zip file that contains a jpg that I am supposed to investigate for the flag.

# Solution
I used the webshell provided from picoctf for this challenge. Here are the following commands I used for the file
''' wget https://artifacts.picoctf.net/c_titan/5/unknown.zip '''
this allowed me to download the file to my linux machine
''' unzip unknown.zip '''
I unzipped the file that was downloaded which then gave me the jpg file "ukn_reality.jpg"
''' file ukn_reality.jpg '''
This was the first command I used but it did not provide as much information that I needed.
''' identify -verbose ukn_reality.jpg '''
This command allowed me detailed information about the image like the dimensions, resolution, color space but it did not have
anything that looked familiar that I thought I needed to find the flag
''' exiftool ukn_reality.jpg '''
This command displays detailed metadata information embedded in the jpg like such as camera settings, creation date, GPS coordinates (if available), and more.
In the details, the attribution url caught my eye because it looked like base64 text.
Attribution Url: cGljb0NURntNRTc0RDQ3QV9ISUREM05fNGRhYmRkY2J9Cg==
I copied the url and decoded it in a base64 decipher and it gave me the flag

flag: picoCTF{ME74D47A_HIDD3N_4dabddcb}
